---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How to get listed"
  description="How to get a Magento or Mage-OS module listed in the Mage-OS Extension Directory."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>How to get listed</h1>
    <p>
      The directory's universe is exactly <a href="https://package-maven.com/" rel="noopener">PackageMaven</a>'s
      index. If your module is in PackageMaven, it shows up here automatically the next time the
      pipeline runs; there's no separate submission to this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Publish on Packagist.</strong> Your module needs a public Composer package name
        (<code>vendor/module-name</code>) on <a href="https://packagist.org/" rel="noopener">Packagist</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Submit to PackageMaven.</strong> Use the "Submit a Module" form on{' '}
        <a href="https://package-maven.com/" rel="noopener">package-maven.com</a>. PackageMaven
        tests each module against real Magento versions and produces the quality tier, PHPStan
        level, and build status shown on every listing here.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Optional: request a vendor trust file.</strong> Partner tiers, editorial picks
        and warnings come from a curated overlay maintained in this repository. Open a pull
        request against{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/mage-os-lab/directory" rel="noopener">the GitHub repository</a>{' '}
        adding or editing <code>data/vendors/&lt;vendor&gt;.json</code>. Read the{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/mage-os-lab/directory/blob/main/docs/trust-policy.md"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          trust policy
        </a>{' '}
        first. It covers vendor identity verification and how editorial picks are kept
        independent of partnership.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the badges mean</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Partner tier</strong> (platinum / gold / silver / bronze) reflects a relationship
        with the Mage-OS organization, which <strong>may be commercial</strong>. It adds a small,
        fixed, published weight to the ranking score, and has no other effect on placement.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Editors&rsquo; pick</strong> is a maintainer judgment about quality or usefulness,
        independent of partner status. Being a partner does not make a package more likely to be
        picked.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Warnings and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      Curators can attach warnings to a listing (info, derank, or hide severity) when there's a
      documented problem, such as an unmaintained package or a security advisory. Any
      <code>derank</code> or <code>hide</code> warning must link public evidence, and (outside a
      security emergency) the vendor is notified with a response window before it merges. If you
      believe a warning on your package is wrong or resolved, open an issue or a counter-PR with
      evidence; a maintainer who wasn't involved in the original warning reviews the dispute. Full
      details live in the{' '}
      <a
        href="https://github.com/mage-os-lab/directory/blob/main/docs/trust-policy.md"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        trust policy
      </a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
